// CROWN — one HOF parameter reaches the frame by two install paths — one under a
// handler that drops the thunk, one under a handler that calls it. The
// thunk's instance must meet the CALLING handler's on its own path.
// Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean and ran at 7 through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23,
// refuter rv3a). Merging the two paths' masks by name keeps one instance
// and loses the other's unification.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect Run { run(f: () -> Int) -> Int }
handler skip { run(f) => resume(0) }
handler call { run(f) => resume(f()) }
fn g(b) = ((b()) ~> skip) + ((b()) ~> call)
fn bad() with !E = g(() => run(() => op()))
handler eh { op() => resume(7) }
fn main() = (bad()) ~> eh
